.TH IPHONEBRIDGE-UI 1 "@DATE@" "iphonebridge @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
iphonebridge-ui \- desktop app for iphonebridge
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B iphonebridge-ui
.SH DESCRIPTION
Graphical front end for
.BR iphonebridge (1):
conversations, the per\-app notification feed, calls, and service
status. It is a separate process talking to the daemon over D\-Bus, so
closing it leaves messages, notifications and calls still arriving. It
is not single\-instance; a second invocation opens a second window.
.PP
In the notification feed, hovering a card reveals a dismiss button
(also on right\-click). Dismissing sends the ANCS negative action, so
the notification clears from the iPhone as well when it is still
current there; older cards are removed from this computer only.
Notifications cleared on the iPhone disappear from the feed likewise.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B IPHONEBRIDGE_UI_DIAG
When set, logs which conversation is open and how arriving messages are
filed, as redacted digests, to
.IR ~/.local/state/iphonebridge/ui-diag.log .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR iphonebridge (1)
